            <ArticleTitle>Antiobesity drugs in the management of type 2 diabetes: A shift in thinking?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S39-S46</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.84.s1.05</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Antiobesity medications can improve metabolic control for patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM) and obesity, but are underutilized. In this review, we describe the role of antiobesity drugs in the context of medically supervised and comprehensive weight-loss interventions and propose a pragmatic therapeutic algorithm for patients with type 2 DM and obesity that incorporates the use of antiobesity drugs early in the course of management.</AbstractText>
